export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=&quot;/path/to/service-account.json&quot;
</code></pre>

Q: Use last inserted id to insert query A: <p>With the below code you can get the last inserted id, so you need use it after your 1st insert and before your 2nd insert.</p>

<pre><code>$insert_id = $this-&gt;db-&gt;insert_id();
</code></pre>

<p>An example would be:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;?php   
$this-&gt;db-&gt;query("INSERT INTO customer (email) values ('".$this-&gt;db-&gt;escape($data['email']."')";
$insert_id = $this-&gt;db-&gt;insert_id();
$this-&gt;db-&gt;query("INSERT INTO `order` (customer_id) values ({$insert_id})";
?&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>$insert_id is an integer, so you dont need to escape it again.
order is a reserved word though, so you might want to change your table name.</p>
